+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and the account settings page (`/account`) support passkeys (WebAuthn):
+
+- **Sign in** – passkeys appear in the username field's autofill, or via “Sign in with a passkey”. After a password sign-in, a passkey is created automatically where the browser supports conditional create.
+- **Sign up** – new accounts are offered a passkey immediately after registration.
+- **Account settings** – list, create, rename and remove passkeys, and edit the display name. Removing a passkey requires a recent passkey reauthentication (5 minutes). Changes are synced to password managers with the WebAuthn Signal API where available.
+
+Server-side verification uses [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/). Configuration (all optional):
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `PASSKEY_RP_ID` | request hostname | Relying Party ID that passkeys are bound to |
+| `PASSKEY_ORIGINS` | request origin (+ `https://` variant) | Comma-separated origins accepted during verification |
+| `PASSKEY_DATA_FILE` | `.data/passkeys.json` | JSON file storing users and passkey public keys |
+
+Password sign-in/registration is proxied through `/api/auth/login` and `/api/auth/register` so that a server session is established for the passkey endpoints.
